                    {
                        "sense_id": "19487c3c-0096-3201-9c1e-396eff4801ee",
                        "entry_id": "9a6eee56-0637-3ac8-8c5c-6a3dd4e1d7a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "jemand, der sich der Alchemie verschreibt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7bca9746-eab0-4b2e-89b8-4c692ac71bca",
                                "sense_id": "19487c3c-0096-3201-9c1e-396eff4801ee",
                                "text": "Athanor ist ein spezieller Ofentyp der Alchemisten."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56e4a671-1614-4933-baf7-740d1954a359",
                                "sense_id": "19487c3c-0096-3201-9c1e-396eff4801ee",
                                "text": "Wichtige Grundlage und sozusagen die Bibel der Alchemisten war die Tabula Smaragdina."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9ee0a4b2-49b9-4b2c-a63a-fa20e6a8fad7",
                        "source_entry_id": "9a6eee56-0637-3ac8-8c5c-6a3dd4e1d7a2",
                        "source_sense_id": "19487c3c-0096-3201-9c1e-396eff4801ee",
                        "source_sense_description": "jemand, der sich der Alchemie verschreibt",
                        "target_lang_word": "炼金术士",
                        "target_lang_code": "zh",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a951dda0-1e94-4311-b46c-3dcf5c40fd1b",
                        "source_entry_id": "9a6eee56-0637-3ac8-8c5c-6a3dd4e1d7a2",
                        "source_sense_id": "19487c3c-0096-3201-9c1e-396eff4801ee",
                        "source_sense_description": "jemand, der sich der Alchemie verschreibt",
                        "target_lang_word": "alchemist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alchemist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c7052ab-6259-386f-ab02-ddf329f245dc",
                                        "entry_id": "2e38022b-e5b7-3b7c-b6ee-51b13e52cae8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who practices alchemy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86456ab7-1cb9-4bdd-ac21-cfde9c72b397",
                                                "sense_id": "1c7052ab-6259-386f-ab02-ddf329f245dc",
                                                "text": "[K]nowledge of philtres, aphrodisiacs, and other sexual stimulants spread from the Arabs and the Moors, from Egypt and India into the European herbals, pharmacopeias, and apothecaries’ lore, and, on a more indeterminate level, among alchemists, wizards, and occultists."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21254feb-cd5a-453c-8a94-8bf8247fcb46",
                                                "sense_id": "1c7052ab-6259-386f-ab02-ddf329f245dc",
                                                "text": "Years later, scientists learned that the sun’s light—visible and invisible—is merely the by-product of a process alchemists had vainly tried to reproduce for centuries—the transmutation of one element into another. That nature accomplishes this before our very eyes, and that it is what creates the solar heat and light that supports all life, was suspected by no one. The revelation came as a complete surprise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad03fc30-1411-3a03-aca1-44a8c405f135",
                                        "entry_id": "2e38022b-e5b7-3b7c-b6ee-51b13e52cae8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who blends material or substances in the nature or supposed nature of alchemy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1c8c7080-a143-4757-96f5-2d2b19b1c93b",
                        "source_entry_id": "9a6eee56-0637-3ac8-8c5c-6a3dd4e1d7a2",
                        "source_sense_id": "19487c3c-0096-3201-9c1e-396eff4801ee",
                        "source_sense_description": "jemand, der sich der Alchemie verschreibt",
                        "target_lang_word": "alchimiste",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alchimiste",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "94546d7c-203e-3c8e-9434-f6f78b2a316f",
                                        "entry_id": "b56bebbd-e3e1-3b85-aa58-f7fdaefdc363",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Celui qui s’occupait d’alchimie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b49c466-52b7-49df-8f55-879950dfbeb0",
                                                "sense_id": "94546d7c-203e-3c8e-9434-f6f78b2a316f",
                                                "text": "[…] ; mais sache, […], que ton père est déjà entre les mains d’un puissant alchimiste qui sait convertir en or et en argent jusqu’aux barres rouillées d’une grille de cachot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35597e5d-5dd9-4dd3-9239-0ddf6391eb6a",
                                                "sense_id": "94546d7c-203e-3c8e-9434-f6f78b2a316f",
                                                "text": "Pendant longtemps, on n’employa qu’en médecine ce liquide qu'on croyait doué de propriétés merveilleuses et qu’on regardait comme une panacée universelle ; c'est ce qui justifie le nom d’aqua vitæ ou eau-de-vie qui lui fut donné par les alchimistes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9abcff0-45b0-40c5-9ef7-3a050cc01ab3",
                                                "sense_id": "94546d7c-203e-3c8e-9434-f6f78b2a316f",
                                                "text": "J’accepte, curieux de faire la connaissance de cet étrange visiteur, et ne tarde pas à apprendre qu’il a été, pendant de longues années, l’astronome-astrologue et l’alchimiste attitré de Mouley El-Hassan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5884503-b14b-41df-862f-991b8e4161bb",
                                                "sense_id": "94546d7c-203e-3c8e-9434-f6f78b2a316f",
                                                "text": "Aux yeux des autorités, être philosophe n’est pas un crime, pratiquer l’alchimie est passible de mort."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7691c639-be99-4f68-8f2e-fbb42f0aa5f8",
                        "source_entry_id": "9a6eee56-0637-3ac8-8c5c-6a3dd4e1d7a2",
